{"name":"Alucard’s Night","hex":"#000055","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"}],"entries":[{"title":"Alucard (Castlevania)","blocks":[{"text":"Adrian Fahrenheit Țepeș , better known as Alucard , is a character in Konami's Castlevania series of video games. His first appearance in the series was in the 1989 game Castlevania III: Dracula's Curse, but he is best known for his role in the critically acclaimed Castlevania: Symphony of the Night, released in 1997. His design in Symphony of the Night was created by Ayami Kojima, marking her first contribution to the Castlevania franchise."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/Alucard-sotn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alucard_(Castlevania)","wikidata":"Q2840528"},{"title":"Alucard (Hellsing)","blocks":[{"text":"Alucard , previously Count Dracula , is a fictional character and the protagonist of the Hellsing manga and anime series created by Kouta Hirano. A vampire devoted entirely to the current head of the Hellsing family, Integra Hellsing, Alucard works with the Hellsing Organization against other vampires and evil forces, fighting with ferocity and cruelty, sometimes only killing after a target has been disabled and humiliated."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Hellsingalucard.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alucard_(Hellsing)","wikidata":"Q282514"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/Alucard-sotn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/eb/Alucard-sotn.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlucard-sotn.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/10.5.17KojiIgarashiPortraitByLuigiNovi1.jpg/500px-10.5.17KojiIgarashiPortraitByLuigiNovi1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/10.5.17KojiIgarashiPortraitByLuigiNovi1.jpg/1280px-10.5.17KojiIgarashiPortraitByLuigiNovi1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/10.5.17KojiIgarashiPortraitByLuigiNovi1.jpg/500px-10.5.17KojiIgarashiPortraitByLuigiNovi1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Game designer Koji Igarashi oversaw several changes for Alucard for his role in Symphony of the Night onwards.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A10.5.17